"\nfile_issue_command = \"python3 .attavo/bin/file-issue\"\n\n[executor]\nbuild = \"claude-code\"\nverify = \"codex\"\n\n[executor.claude-code]\nauth = \"subscription\"\nmodel = \"claude-sonnet-5\"\n\n[executor.codex]\nmodel = \"gpt-5.6-sol\"\n\n[spec]\n[spec.boundary]\npaths = [\"bin/**\", \"adapters/**\", \"schema/**\", \"templates/**\", \"action.yml\", \"scripts/**\"]\n\n[gates]\n[gates.spec]\ncommand = \"attavo spec-gate\"\nretires = [\n  \"the lane as the product's transport: a Claude Code lane session reporting to a reviewing session, with no spec, no approval bound to a commit, no build/verify separation, and no attestation on the product's own commits\",\n  \"the || true step in ci.yml that ran the doctor's four proofs against this repository expected to still fail\",\n  \"the reviewing session as the reader of whether the lane did what the issue said\",\n]\n\n[tests]\nselect = \"python3 .attavo/bin/select-tests\"\nrun = \"xargs -r python3 -m pytest -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\"\n\n[paths]\nspecs = \"attest/specs\"\nrecords = \"attest/records\"\nrulings = \"attest/rulings.md\"\nrejections = \"attest/rejections\"\n\n[operators]\napprovers = [\"dbean10\"]\n\n[checks]\ncommand = \"python3 -m pytest tests -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' attest/specs/148/spec.md\nsed -n '1,220p' attest/specs/148/criteria/proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh\nsed -n '1,160p' attest/specs/148/criteria/doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh\nsed -n '1,240p' attest/rulings.md\nsed -n '280,330p' bin/attavo\nsed -n '850,980p' bin/attavo\nsed -n '1,240p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch | head -240\nrg -n \\\"ordinary_commits|unrecorded_commits|proof_no_commit_lacks_record|test_doctor|diff --git|no-cause|stop|class\\\" /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch attest/records/148/build-01.log | head -240\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' attest/specs/148/spec.md\nsed -n '1,220p' attest/specs/148/criteria/proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh\nsed -n '1,160p' attest/specs/148/criteria/doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh\nsed -n '1,240p' attest/rulings.md\nsed -n '280,330p' bin/attavo\nsed -n '850,980p' bin/attavo\nsed -n '1,240p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch | head -240\nrg -n \\\"ordinary_commits|unrecorded_commits|proof_no_commit_lacks_record|test_doctor|diff --git|no-cause|stop|class\\\" /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch attest/records/148/build-01.log | head -240\"","aggregated_output":"## Problem\n\n`attavo doctor`'s third proof classes every first-parent commit on the tenant's `main` since the install as recorded, ordinary, or unrecorded, and its JSON entry carries the three counts and the boundary-evasion count (issue #72): the governed-versus-ordinary path ratio the operator screen renders. It carries no lists, so a reader of the ratio cannot see which merges arrived outside an item (a pin, a lane, a signal branch) or which commits lack a record; the only way to name them is to re-run the classification by hand with `git rev-list` against the records, which is the doctor's job.\n\nRetires: the by-hand `git rev-list --first-parent` read of the ordinary merges, and the screen's ratio as a number with nothing behind it.\n\n## Claims\n\n- bin/attavo\n- tests/test_doctor.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh: on a three-way fixture tenant the script builds with git, attavo doctor --json carries ordinary_commits and unrecorded_commits on proof three, each commit with sha and subject, the ordinary merge flagged as a boundary evasion\n- doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh: bin/attavo emits the two list keys by name\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nhere=$(pwd)\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\ncd \"$tmp\"\ngit init -q -b main .\ngit config user.email doctor@attavo.invalid\ngit config user.name \"doctor fixture\"\nprintf '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[spec.boundary]\\npaths = [\"boundary/**\"]\\n' > attavo.toml\ngit add attavo.toml\ngit commit -q -m install\ngit checkout -q -b attavo/1-x\nmkdir -p records/1\nprintf '{\"status\": \"pass\"}' > records/1/spec-01.json\ngit add records\ngit commit -q -m \"spec record for item 1\"\ngit checkout -q main\ngit merge -q --no-ff -m \"Merge branch 'attavo/1-x'\" attavo/1-x\ngit checkout -q -b ordinary-change\nmkdir -p boundary\nprintf 'v2\\n' > boundary/thing.txt\ngit add boundary\ngit commit -q -m \"an ordinary change\"\ngit checkout -q main\ngit merge -q --no-ff -m \"Merge branch 'ordinary-change'\" ordinary-change\nprintf 'direct\\n' > direct.txt\ngit add direct.txt\ngit commit -q -m \"a change committed straight to main\"\ncd \"$here\"\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" > \"$tmp/doctor.json\" || true\npython3 - \"$tmp/doctor.json\" <<'PY'\nimport json, sys\nd = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\np = [x for x in d[\"proofs\"] if x[\"proof\"] == \"no-commit-lacks-record\"][0]\nassert p[\"ordinary\"] == 1 and p[\"unrecorded\"] == 1, p\no = p[\"ordinary_commits\"]\nu = p[\"unrecorded_commits\"]\nassert [c[\"subject\"] for c in o] == [\"Merge branch 'ordinary-change'\"], o\nassert o[0][\"boundary_evasion\"] is True and len(o[0][\"sha\"]) == 40, o\nassert [c[\"subject\"] for c in u] == [\"a change committed straight to main\"], u\nPY\n#!/bin/sh\ngrep -q '\"ordinary_commits\"' bin/attavo && grep -q '\"unrecorded_commits\"' bin/attavo\n# Rulings\n\nWritten by the merge of a proposed amendment only.\ndef drive_forge_poll_bound_s() -> float:\n    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S))\n\n\ndef drive_forge_poll_interval_s() -> float:\n    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S))\n\n\nclass Proof:\n    def __init__(self, key: str, title: str) -> None:\n        self.key = key\n        self.title = title\n        self.holds = False\n        self.reason = \"\"\n        self.extra: dict = {}\n\n    def fail(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \"Proof\":\n        self.holds, self.reason = False, reason\n        self.extra.update(extra)\n        return self\n\n    def hold(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \"Proof\":\n        self.holds, self.reason = True, reason\n        self.extra.update(extra)\n        return self\n\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\"proof\": self.key, \"title\": self.title,\n                \"holds\": self.holds, \"reason\": self.reason, **self.extra}\n\n\ndef read_manifest(root: Path) -> dict | None:\n    path = root / MANIFEST\n    if not path.is_file():\n        return None\n    with path.open(\"rb\") as fh:\n        return tomllib.load(fh)\n\n\ndef git(root: Path, *args: str, env: dict | None = None) -> str:\n    out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), *args],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\n    if out.returncode != 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(out.stderr.strip() or \"git failed\")\n    return out.stdout\n\n\ndef product_version() -> str:\n    \"\"\"What the running program is. Three fallbacks, in order, and never an\n    exception -- this runs inside write_record, after the work it\n    describes already happened, and a raise here would lose the record\n\ndef touches_boundary(root: Path, sha: str, boundary_paths: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Whether sha's first-parent diff touches a path [spec.boundary].paths\n    declares governed -- an ordinary merge that does is a boundary\n    evasion (issue #72): the tenant carried a governed change around the\n    path the manifest itself names.\"\"\"\n    diff = git(root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", f\"{sha}^1\", sha).splitlines()\n    return any(fnmatch.fnmatch(path, pattern) for path in diff for pattern in boundary_paths)\n\n\ndef proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"no-commit-lacks-record\", \"no commit lacks a record\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; the tenant has no record boundary\")\n    try:\n        install = git(root, \"log\", \"--diff-filter=A\", \"--format=%H\",\n                      \"--reverse\", \"--\", MANIFEST).split()\n    except RuntimeError as exc:\n        return p.fail(f\"git: {exc}\")\n    if not install:\n        return p.fail(f\"{MANIFEST} is not committed; the tenant has no record boundary\")\n    install_sha = install[0]\n    full_chain = git(root, \"rev-list\", f\"{install_sha}..HEAD\", \"--first-parent\").split()\n    if not full_chain:\n        return p.fail(f\"no commit after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}; nothing has been recorded\")\n\n    # issue #74: [doctor] from lets a tenant declare the doctor's read to\n    # start at a later commit on main's first-parent line -- the point\n    # after which every push arrived through the queue -- rather than the\n    # install commit, which on a repository that adopted the product\n    # after its history began is a boundary the doctor cannot otherwise\n    # see. Any spelling git resolves is accepted (a short sha, a tag, a\n    # ref) -- resolved with rev-parse --verify before the first-parent\n    # check runs, so the two failure modes stay distinct: a spelling that\n    # names no commit at all, and a commit that names one off the line.\n    # Checked, not trusted: neither is silently forgiven back to install.\n    declared_from = (m.get(\"doctor\") or {}).get(\"from\")\n    window_start = install_sha\n    if declared_from is not None:\n        try:\n            resolved_from = git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", f\"{declared_from}^{{commit}}\").strip()\n        except RuntimeError:\n            return p.fail(f\"[doctor] from {declared_from} does not resolve to a commit\")\n        if resolved_from != install_sha and resolved_from not in full_chain:\n            return p.fail(f\"[doctor] from {declared_from} is not on main's first-parent \"\n                          f\"line after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}\")\n        window_start = resolved_from\n\n    if window_start == install_sha:\n        window_spec = f\"{install_sha}..HEAD\"\n        commits = full_chain\n    else:\n        window_spec = f\"{window_start}^..HEAD\"\n        commits = git(root, \"rev-list\", window_spec, \"--first-parent\").split()\n    before_window = len(full_chain) - len(commits)\n\n    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\n    named: set[str] = set()\n    for stages in load_records(records_dir).values():\n        for rec in stages.values():\n            sha = rec.get(\"sha\")\n            if isinstance(sha, str):\n                named.add(sha)\n            for c in rec.get(\"commits\", []) or []:\n                if isinstance(c, str):\n                    named.add(c)\n    record_commits = set(git(root, \"rev-list\", window_spec, \"--first-parent\",\n                             \"--\", records_rel).split()) if records_rel else set()\n    merges = set(git(root, \"rev-list\", window_spec, \"--first-parent\", \"--merges\").split())\n    boundary_paths = ((m.get(\"spec\") or {}).get(\"boundary\") or {}).get(\"paths\") or []\n\n    # Every first-parent commit in the window is exactly one of three\n    # (issue #72): recorded (a record names it, or its diff touches\n    # paths.records), ordinary (a merge that doesn't), or unrecorded\n    # (anything else -- on a protected main with a queue, a non-merge\n    # commit is the only way a change arrives without the forge).\n    recorded, ordinary, unrecorded = [], [], []\n    boundary_evasions = 0\n    evasion_shas: set[str] = set()\n    for c in commits:\n        if c in named or c in record_commits:\n            recorded.append(c)\n        elif c in merges:\n            ordinary.append(c)\n            if boundary_paths and touches_boundary(root, c, boundary_paths):\n                boundary_evasions += 1\n                evasion_shas.add(c)\n        else:\n            unrecorded.append(c)\n\n    def commit_entries(shas: list[str]) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"sha and subject for each of shas, in the order given -- a reader\n        of the ratio names the commits behind it without re-running the\n        classification by hand (issue #148).\"\"\"\n        if not shas:\n            return []\n        out = git(root, \"log\", \"--no-walk\", \"--format=%H\\x1f%s\", *shas)\n        return [{\"sha\": sha, \"subject\": subject}\n                for sha, subject in (line.split(\"\\x1f\", 1) for line in out.splitlines())]\n\n    ordinary_commits = commit_entries(ordinary)\n    for entry in ordinary_commits:\n        entry[\"boundary_evasion\"] = entry[\"sha\"] in evasion_shas\n    unrecorded_commits = commit_entries(unrecorded)\n\n    counts = f\"{len(recorded)} recorded, {len(ordinary)} ordinary, {len(unrecorded)} unrecorded\"\n    evasions = boundary_evasions if boundary_paths else \"n/a\"\n    extra = {\"recorded\": len(recorded), \"ordinary\": len(ordinary),\n             \"unrecorded\": len(unrecorded), \"boundary_evasions\": evasions,\n             \"before_window\": before_window,\n             \"ordinary_commits\": ordinary_commits, \"unrecorded_commits\": unrecorded_commits}\n    if unrecorded:\n        return p.fail(f\"{unrecorded[-1][:12]} lacks a record; {counts}; boundary evasions: \"\n                      f\"{evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\", **extra)\n    return p.hold(f\"{counts}; boundary evasions: {evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\",\n                  **extra)\n\n\nADAPTER_EXIT_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\[adapter exited \\d+\\]$\")\n\n\ndef _log_owes_tool_error(log: str | None) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True when a log's last non-empty line is exactly an adapter-exit\n    marker and every line before it parses as JSON -- an adapter's own\n    event stream, never a tool's own words (issue #94's own specimen,\n    tenant zero's attest/records/659/verify-01.log: codex's\n    \"thread.started\" event, then nothing but \"[adapter exited 1]\" -- the\n    tool's real error line dropped before this reached the log, issue\n    #86's own bug in split_adapter_stdout). A log that is only the exit\n    marker, nothing before it at all, still owes the same line.\"\"\"\ndiff --git a/attest/records/148/approval-01.json b/attest/records/148/approval-01.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..bf8583a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/records/148/approval-01.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+{\n+  \"sha\": \"2297cf56007c2948ef567defe3a751dc0910a1fc\",\n+  \"spec_sha\": \"258287507e7d784861221ac62b3680ab43e85c10\",\n+  \"approved_by\": \"dbean10\",\n+  \"at\": \"2026-09-17T12:33:55Z\",\n+  \"record_version\": 2,\n+  \"item\": \"148\",\n+  \"product_version\": \"v0.25.0\",\n+  \"product_pin\": \"v0.25.0\"\n+}\ndiff --git a/attest/records/148/spec-01.json b/attest/records/148/spec-01.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ffe0118\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/records/148/spec-01.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+{\n+  \"sha\": \"258287507e7d784861221ac62b3680ab43e85c10\",\n+  \"spec_sha\": \"258287507e7d784861221ac62b3680ab43e85c10\",\n+  \"at\": \"2026-09-17T12:27:01Z\",\n+  \"status\": \"pass\",\n+  \"approval_sha\": null,\n+  \"criteria\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh\",\n+      \"on_tree\": 1,\n+      \"on_stub\": 0\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh\",\n+      \"on_tree\": 1,\n+      \"on_stub\": 0\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"refusal\": null,\n+  \"record_version\": 2,\n+  \"item\": \"148\",\n+  \"product_version\": \"v0.25.0\",\n+  \"product_pin\": \"v0.25.0\"\n+}\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/148/criteria/doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh b/attest/specs/148/criteria/doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh\nnew file mode 100755\nindex 0000000..4473091\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/specs/148/criteria/doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\n+#!/bin/sh\n+grep -q '\"ordinary_commits\"' bin/attavo && grep -q '\"unrecorded_commits\"' bin/attavo\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/148/criteria/proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh b/attest/specs/148/criteria/proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh\nnew file mode 100755\nindex 0000000..2f8fae0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/specs/148/criteria/proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+#!/bin/sh\n+set -e\n+here=$(pwd)\n+tmp=$(mktemp -d)\n+cd \"$tmp\"\n+git init -q -b main .\n+git config user.email doctor@attavo.invalid\n+git config user.name \"doctor fixture\"\n+printf '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[spec.boundary]\\npaths = [\"boundary/**\"]\\n' > attavo.toml\n+git add attavo.toml\n+git commit -q -m install\n+git checkout -q -b attavo/1-x\n+mkdir -p records/1\n+printf '{\"status\": \"pass\"}' > records/1/spec-01.json\n+git add records\n+git commit -q -m \"spec record for item 1\"\n+git checkout -q main\n+git merge -q --no-ff -m \"Merge branch 'attavo/1-x'\" attavo/1-x\n+git checkout -q -b ordinary-change\n+mkdir -p boundary\n+printf 'v2\\n' > boundary/thing.txt\n+git add boundary\n+git commit -q -m \"an ordinary change\"\n+git checkout -q main\n+git merge -q --no-ff -m \"Merge branch 'ordinary-change'\" ordinary-change\n+printf 'direct\\n' > direct.txt\n+git add direct.txt\n+git commit -q -m \"a change committed straight to main\"\n+cd \"$here\"\n+python3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" > \"$tmp/doctor.json\" || true\n+python3 - \"$tmp/doctor.json\" <<'PY'\n+import json, sys\n+d = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\n+p = [x for x in d[\"proofs\"] if x[\"proof\"] == \"no-commit-lacks-record\"][0]\n+assert p[\"ordinary\"] == 1 and p[\"unrecorded\"] == 1, p\n+o = p[\"ordinary_commits\"]\n+u = p[\"unrecorded_commits\"]\n+assert [c[\"subject\"] for c in o] == [\"Merge branch 'ordinary-change'\"], o\n+assert o[0][\"boundary_evasion\"] is True and len(o[0][\"sha\"]) == 40, o\n+assert [c[\"subject\"] for c in u] == [\"a change committed straight to main\"], u\n+PY\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/148/spec.md b/attest/specs/148/spec.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..71e87f4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/specs/148/spec.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+## Problem\n+\n+`attavo doctor`'s third proof classes every first-parent commit on the tenant's `main` since the install as recorded, ordinary, or unrecorded, and its JSON entry carries the three counts and the boundary-evasion count (issue #72): the governed-versus-ordinary path ratio the operator screen renders. It carries no lists, so a reader of the ratio cannot see which merges arrived outside an item (a pin, a lane, a signal branch) or which commits lack a record; the only way to name them is to re-run the classification by hand with `git rev-list` against the records, which is the doctor's job.\n+\n+Retires: the by-hand `git rev-list --first-parent` read of the ordinary merges, and the screen's ratio as a number with nothing behind it.\n+\n+## Claims\n+\n+- bin/attavo\n+- tests/test_doctor.py\n+\n+## Criteria\n+\n+- proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh: on a three-way fixture tenant the script builds with git, attavo doctor --json carries ordinary_commits and unrecorded_commits on proof three, each commit with sha and subject, the ordinary merge flagged as a boundary evasion\n+- doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh: bin/attavo emits the two list keys by name\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/148/stub/bin/attavo b/attest/specs/148/stub/bin/attavo\nnew file mode 100755\nindex 0000000..f5da634\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/specs/148/stub/bin/attavo\n@@ -0,0 +1,3399 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"attavo: the command.\n+\n+    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\n+    attavo spec-gate [N]\n+    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\n+    attavo approval-status [N]\n+    attavo build [N]\n+    attavo verify [N]\n+    attavo file-findings [N]\n+    attavo file-stops [N]\n+    attavo counsel [N]\n+    attavo record-only\n+    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n+    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready]\n+    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n+    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n+\n+The doctor is the definition of done. It asserts four proofs against a\n+tenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n+\n+  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n+                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n+                             and carries a non-empty retires\n+  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n+                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n+                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n+                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n+  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n+                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n+                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n+                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n+                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n+                             carries its own record paths this way)\n+  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n+                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n+                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n+                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n+                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n+                             heading when a build failed after running\n+                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n+                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n+                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n+                             never refused\n+\n+Nothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\n+blocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\n+is done.\n+\n+spec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\n+from the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\n+is read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\n+branch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\n+rejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\n+even while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\n+branch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\n+file under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\n+the spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\n+one enforces.\n+\n+build refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\n+declares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\n+approval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n+(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\n+GIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\n+config, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\n+spec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\n+between start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\n+every path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\n+declared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\n+it can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\n+never supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\n+silent null -- then runs the criteria, the\n+tests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\n+when the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\n+whole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\n+the test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\n+non-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\n+budget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\n+refused. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\n+the adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\n+exits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\n+under an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\n+it as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n+{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\n+already on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\n+build contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\n+enforces.\n+\n+verify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\n+status pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\n+a tenant command, taking a full commit sha on argv, that prints one\n+line per check as \"<name> <conclusion>\". verify runs it on the build\n+record's sha first: any conclusion other than success, neutral, or\n+skipped writes verify-NN.json with status returned and calls no\n+adapter, because a judge is never spent on a tree the forge already\n+called red. With the forge green, verify calls the adapter named by\n+[executor].verify (defaulting to [executor].build) with the diff since\n+the build's approval, the spec, and the build record, and records its\n+findings and its declared \"reports\" (issue #41). [executor.<adapter>.<stage>] shadows [executor.<adapter>] for\n+build or verify alone; both merge parent then stage before setting\n+ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the record's adapter_config is the merged\n+result. Like build, every verify record whose status is not pass\n+carries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\n+carries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\n+the item's latest verify record via [forge].file_issue_command, and\n+refuses (exit 1, nothing filed) a record carrying a finding with no\n+retires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\n+full rules both enforce.\n+\n+file-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\n+issue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1:diff --git a/attest/records/148/approval-01.json b/attest/records/148/approval-01.json\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:17:diff --git a/attest/records/148/spec-01.json b/attest/records/148/spec-01.json\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:47:diff --git a/attest/specs/148/criteria/doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh b/attest/specs/148/criteria/doctor-names-the-list-keys.sh\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:54:+grep -q '\"ordinary_commits\"' bin/attavo && grep -q '\"unrecorded_commits\"' bin/attavo\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:55:diff --git a/attest/specs/148/criteria/proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh b/attest/specs/148/criteria/proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:96:+o = p[\"ordinary_commits\"]\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:97:+u = p[\"unrecorded_commits\"]\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:102:diff --git a/attest/specs/148/spec.md b/attest/specs/148/spec.md\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:110:+`attavo doctor`'s third proof classes every first-parent commit on the tenant's `main` since the install as recorded, ordinary, or unrecorded, and its JSON entry carries the three counts and the boundary-evasion count (issue #72): the governed-versus-ordinary path ratio the operator screen renders. It carries no lists, so a reader of the ratio cannot see which merges arrived outside an item (a pin, a lane, a signal branch) or which commits lack a record; the only way to name them is to re-run the classification by hand with `git rev-list` against the records, which is the doctor's job.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:117:+- tests/test_doctor.py\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:121:+- proof-three-json-lists-the-commits.sh: on a three-way fixture tenant the script builds with git, attavo doctor --json carries ordinary_commits and unrecorded_commits on proof three, each commit with sha and subject, the ordinary merge flagged as a boundary evasion\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:123:diff --git a/attest/specs/148/stub/bin/attavo b/attest/specs/148/stub/bin/attavo\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:139:+    attavo file-stops [N]\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:145:+    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:163:+  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:165:+                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:166:+                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:167:+                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:212:+it as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:213:+{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:214:+already on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:232:+carries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:233:+carries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:239:+file-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:241:+class, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:247:+nothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:248:+empty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:260:+same sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:261:+stop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:311:+and performs the next mechanical step, and only that step, then stops: no\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:316:+and stops there -- the merge is never drive's own act, and it enqueues\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:318:+issue #100) and filed (file-stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:326:+same stop, reading exactly what the prior run left behind -- the marker\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:327:+included, so a stop already filed is never filed again, from this\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:334:+passing step, until the item is ready to merge or a step stops on its\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:336:+forge never going green); a step that stops still prints exactly what\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:338:+drive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:344:+row per act: the sha, the identity as git names it, and a class from a\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:349:+(record), executor commits (change), stops (non-pass records), and\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:357:+stops reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:359:+record: the record, its stop's class, provenance, and detail, and the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:361:+stop, else \"person\" for a question, else \"guard\" for a class a guard\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:363:+carry stop at all prints the doctor's own phrase for it, \"before stop\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:364:+was recorded\", and is counted there rather than by class. Totals per\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:365:+class (read from the build record schema's own enum, never retyped) and\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:366:+per answerer, plus the before-stop count, follow the rows. --json prints\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:396:+# before it gives up and stops rather than call a judge on a tree the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:416:+class Proof:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:520:+class ShallowCheckoutError(RuntimeError):\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:558:+class RecordItemMismatch(RuntimeError):\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:659:+# --- stop: every non-pass build or verify record's class and cause (issue\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:663:+# exactly a stop the product wrote with nothing beside it to explain\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:666:+STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:667:+               \"ceiling\", \"claims-boundary\", \"repeated-act\", \"unclassed\", \"question\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:673:+# v0.16.0) once put a class's own name, or a real specimen's wording of\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:675:+# moves non-question and outlived-invocation onto report_class instead\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:676:+# (below): non-question's own halt line (\"halted: class non-question\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:679:+# never named its class in text to begin with, so both are disabled here\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:688:+    # default (the class's own name, \"ceiling\"), the generic match above\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:698:+    # Left at the default, the generic match above would misclassify any\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:700:+    # provenance, before the structural check in derive_stop is reached.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:708:+    # check_auth) as an environment/executor stop that never happened.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:724:+# Issue #100's followups: an unclassed detail is the log's last line\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:727:+# at write time, so a filed issue's own summary of it (file-stops'\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:728:+# log_tail already carries the full picture) stays short; the class\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:729:+# itself, \"unclassed\", already says the full explanation lives in the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:740:+def _carries_a_known_class(text: str | None) -> str | None:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:743:+    class is not disabled there -- or None. Issue #88 is where an\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:744:+    adapter's own halt or refusal first named its class this way; issue\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:748:+    both from the adapter's own report line (derive_stop's report_class)\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:758:+def derive_stop(status: str, *, refusal: str | None = None, halted: dict | None = None,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:759:+                log: str | None = None, report_class: str | None = None,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:761:+    \"\"\"The stop field for a build or verify record: None for status \"pass\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:762:+    else {class, provenance, detail} from what the caller already knows.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:764:+      - report_class -- payload.get(\"class\") off the adapter's own report\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:766:+        that class, provenance \"executor\". build.schema.json and\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:768:+        class lives only on the report line, never a structured field\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:775:+        class an adapter does not yet put on its report line --\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:777:+        report line at all -- falls to unclassed below, same as any\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:779:+        class on the line the way non-question already does.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:784:+        retire: tenant zero's #663 build-01, a proper question, classed\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:785:+        unclassed/product and filed as a product defect with the wrong\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:790:+        class in text (issue #88, #93 for ceiling's own pre-emptive\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:791:+        refusal) is that class, provenance \"executor\" -- the log is\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:793:+        class today; the class-naming line each adapter prints reaches\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:807:+      - anything else is unclassed/product, with the log's last line\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:809:+        class that carries a detail, since every remaining class's\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:816:+        return {\"class\": \"forge-unconcluded\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": None}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:817:+    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:818:+        return {\"class\": report_class, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:821:+        return {\"class\": \"question\", \"provenance\": \"spec\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:823:+    known = _carries_a_known_class(refusal) or _carries_a_known_class(log)\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:825:+        return {\"class\": known, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:827:+        return {\"class\": \"claims-boundary\", \"provenance\": refusal_provenance or \"spec\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:830:+        return {\"class\": \"ceiling\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": None}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:831:+    return {\"class\": \"unclassed\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": _log_last_line(log)}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:834:+def gate_stop(refusal: str | None) -> dict:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:835:+    \"\"\"The stop for a refused spec-gate record: class \"gate\", provenance\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:837:+    derive_stop's generic claims-boundary/spec fallback issue #133\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:841:+    a spec record still carries no stop field of its own; this is\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:842:+    synthesized wherever a refused one is read (item_stops,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:843:+    cmd_file_stops, proof_no_stop_lacks_cause), never persisted.\"\"\"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:844:+    return {\"class\": \"gate\", \"provenance\": \"spec\", \"detail\": refusal}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:993:+def proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1084:+             \"ordinary_commits\": [{\"sha\": c, \"subject\": commit_subject(root, c),\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1087:+             \"unrecorded_commits\": [{\"sha\": c, \"subject\": commit_subject(root, c)}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1121:+def proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1122:+    p = Proof(\"no-stop-lacks-cause\", \"no stop lacks its cause\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1131:+    # before record_version 3 has no stop by construction (schema\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1146:+                stop = rec.get(\"stop\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1147:+                if not stop:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1148:+                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} carries no stop\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1150:+                cls, provenance = stop.get(\"class\"), stop.get(\"provenance\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1152:+                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1153:+                                    f\"no enumerated class\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1156:+                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1159:+                if cls == \"unclassed\" and not stop.get(\"detail\"):\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1160:+                    problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is unclassed with no detail\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1168:+                # else stop already says.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1180:+        # issue #137: a refused spec-gate record is a stop too, class\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1181:+        # \"gate\" -- synthesized the same way item_stops and\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1182:+        # cmd_file_stops already read it, since cmd_spec_gate itself\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1183:+        # carries no stop field to check for one. No record_version\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1184:+        # gate here: unlike build/verify's own stop field, gate is never\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1191:+            stop = gate_stop(rec.get(\"refusal\"))\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1192:+            cls, provenance = stop[\"class\"], stop[\"provenance\"]\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1194:+                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1195:+                                f\"no enumerated class\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1198:+                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1201:+            if not stop.get(\"detail\"):\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1202:+                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is a gate stop with no cause\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1204:+    older_note = f\"{older} record(s) before stop was recorded\"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1208:+                 else f\"{checked} non-pass record(s) carry stop with a cause ({older_note})\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1216:+            proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root, m),\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1217:+            proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root, m)]\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1682:+# The stop classes issue #89 gave no code of their own beyond the guard\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1688:+# #115). question (a person's to answer) and the residual (no-cause,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1689:+# unclassed -- nobody has looked yet) are not in this tuple; attavo stops\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1691:+# not beside derive_stop, which never needs to tell a guard from any\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1692:+# other class once it has already named one.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1697:+def stop_class_enum() -> tuple[str, ...]:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1698:+    \"\"\"Every class a stop can name, read from the build record schema's own\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1700:+    once (environment arrived in the schema before anything but derive_stop\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1705:+    return tuple(schema[\"properties\"][\"stop\"][\"properties\"][\"class\"][\"enum\"])\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:1880:+                \"stop\": {\"class\": \"environment\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": detail},\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2074:+        \"stop\": derive_stop(status_out, refusal=refusal, halted=halted,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2076:+                            report_class=(payload or {}).get(\"class\"),\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2117:+    # checks to a pull request's head, and that commit stops being the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2188:+    # executor's own commit -- that commit stops being the head the\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2213:+            \"stop\": derive_stop(\"returned\"),\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2321:+        \"stop\": derive_stop(status_out, log=transcript,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2322:+                            report_class=(payload or {}).get(\"class\")),\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2330:+# --- counsel: a stop is read inside the product first, before a person\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2342:+    a refused gate is the same shape of stop, earlier, and it is read only\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2346:+    \"build, else verify\" so a stop on the stage that ran later (typically\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2384:+    stage, stop_record, record_path = latest_non_pass_stage_record(item_records_dir)\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2385:+    if stop_record is None:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2406:+    diff_text, diff_refusal = diff_since_approval(root, stop_record.get(\"approval_sha\"))\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2455:+        cls = payload.get(\"class\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2475:+        \"class\": cls,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2492:+    \"\"\"Whether poll_forge_checks should keep waiting rather than stop at\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2510:+    concluded, green or not, stops here at once: there is nothing left to\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2533:+    the same filed fact rather than refiling every stop it finds with no\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2619:+    #100) and filed (cmd_file_stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2620:+    so a stop's own counsel record and .filed marker -- the filing\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2621:+    command's stdout, the issue file-stops just opened -- exist on disk\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2625:+    would refile every stop it finds with no marker beside it. The stage\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2649:+        # file-stops is its own idempotent read of the item's records, so\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2651:+        # safe to call again on a later run: an already-filed stop's own\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2652:+        # marker is what stops it from being filed twice.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2653:+        cmd_file_stops([item_id])\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2659:+        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not commit the {stage} record: {exc}\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2664:+        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not push the {stage} record: {err}\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2669:+        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: {stage} halted: {question} ({after.name}); \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2673:+        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: {stage} {status_out}: {reason} ({after.name}); \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2682:+    has -- and whether repetition under --until-ready should stop here:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2683:+    True for every refusal or stop (no valid approval, no\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2714:+        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: forge checks not green on {head_sha[:12]}: {conclusions}\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2744:+    # item is ready to merge or a step stops on its own account.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2805:+# --- file-stops: one tenant issue per stop record, nothing filed silently,\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2812:+def compose_stop_title(item_id: str, stage: str, n: int, stop: dict) -> str:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2813:+    \"\"\"`stop <class>/<provenance> on item <N>: <stage>-<NN>` -- the title\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2815:+    <untitled> for. An empty class or provenance is a record defect, not\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2818:+    cls = stop.get(\"class\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2819:+    provenance = stop.get(\"provenance\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2822:+    return f\"stop {cls}/{provenance} on item {item_id}: {stage}-{n:02d}\"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2829:+    (e.g. file-stops run standalone, outside drive).\"\"\"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2836:+def cmd_file_stops(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2840:+        print(\"attavo file-stops: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2845:+        print(f\"attavo file-stops: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2854:+        print(\"attavo file-stops: refused: no [forge].file_issue_command in the manifest\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2857:+    # A stop record's own .filed marker beside it -- the same convention as\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2871:+            stop = attempts[n].get(\"stop\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2872:+            if not stop:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2877:+            pending.append((stage, n, stop, marker))\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2879:+    # A refused spec-gate record is the same shape of stop, earlier (issue\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2880:+    # #133); its own class is \"gate\" (issue #137), never persisted -- it\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2881:+    # never carries a stop field of its own (cmd_spec_gate is untouched\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2889:+        pending.append((\"spec\", n, gate_stop(rec.get(\"refusal\")), marker))\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2892:+        print(\"attavo file-stops: no stops to file\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2895:+    for stage, n, stop, _marker in pending:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2896:+        if stop[\"class\"] == \"unclassed\" and not stop.get(\"detail\"):\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2897:+            print(f\"attavo file-stops: refused: {stage}-{n:02d} is unclassed with no detail; \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2901:+    for stage, n, stop, _marker in pending:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2902:+        if not compose_stop_title(item_id, stage, n, stop):\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2903:+            print(f\"attavo file-stops: refused: {stage}-{n:02d} composes an empty title; \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2907:+    for stage, n, stop, marker in pending:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2914:+            \"title\": compose_stop_title(item_id, stage, n, stop),\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2915:+            \"class\": stop[\"class\"],\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2916:+            \"provenance\": stop[\"provenance\"],\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2927:+            print(f\"attavo file-stops: refused: filing {stage}-{n:02d} exited {run.returncode}: \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:2932:+    print(f\"attavo file-stops: filed {len(pending)} issue(s)\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3152:+# --- ledger: every act on an item by identity and class (issue #128) ---\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3220:+    Each commit gets exactly one class, in this order: the merge commit\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3240:+                     \"stops\": 0, \"since\": None}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3264:+            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"merge\"})\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3269:+            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"change\"})\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3290:+                rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"approve\"})\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3298:+                rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"record\"})\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3304:+                rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"record-or-launch\",\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3308:+            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"launch\"})\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3314:+            rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": cls})\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3319:+        rows.append({\"sha\": sha, \"identity\": name, \"class\": \"transport\"})\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3322:+    # issue #137: the same set attavo stops counts, from the same reader\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3323:+    # (item_stops) -- not a second, independent count kept in sync by\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3326:+    stops = len(item_stops(root, m, item_id)[\"rows\"])\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3329:+              \"executor_commits\": executor_commits, \"stops\": stops, \"since\": since}\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3363:+            print(f\"  {row['sha'][:12]}  {row['identity']:<32}  {row['class']}{note}\")\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3366:+             f\"executor commits: {s['executor_commits']}  stops: {s['stops']}  \"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3373:+# --- stops: every non-pass record by class, provenance, and answerer\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3376:+def item_stops(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> dict:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3379:+    #133), class \"gate\" (issue #137) -- read from status and refusal\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3380:+    rather than a stop field spec-gate records never carry (gate_stop\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3382:+    record_version -- a record too old to carry stop at all still gets\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3383:+    a row, its class printed as the doctor's own phrase for it.\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3387:+    number -- the product's own answer, which wins over whatever the stop\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3388:+    itself says, since a counseled stop was already read once; failing\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3389:+    that, \"person\" for class question (a person's to answer, not a\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3390:+    guard's); failing that, \"guard\" for a class in GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpg9bjtwl7/diff.patch:3392:+    -- no-cause, unclassed, or no stop at all -- is \"none\": nobody has\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
